  "tempo": 1.12,
  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "That tiny hole in some pen caps can serve a much more serious purpose than you'd",
      "start": 0.039,
      "end": 4.004
    },
    {
      "text": "expect.",
      "start": 4.004,
      "end": 4.469
    },
    {
      "text": "On vented caps, such as the Bic Cristal, the opening is there for safety.",
      "start": 4.782,
      "end": 8.691
    },
    {
      "text": "If someone accidentally inhales the cap and it gets lodged in the airway, the vent",
      "start": 9.007,
      "end": 13.232
    },
    {
      "text": "may still allow some air to pass through while emergency help is needed.",
      "start": 13.232,
      "end": 16.877
    },
    {
      "text": "International safety standards specifically address vented pen caps for",
      "start": 17.201,
      "end": 20.988
    },
    {
      "text": "this reason.",
      "start": 20.988,
      "end": 21.542
    },
    {
      "text": "So one of the cheapest, most forgettable pieces of plastic on your desk has a",
      "start": 21.893,
      "end": 25.618
    },
    {
      "text": "design feature meant for an emergency where a few extra breaths could matter.",
      "start": 25.618,
      "end": 29.285
    }
  ],
